Subject: mrboom.h: big-endian layout for the SDL front ends

The 8086 registers and the string instructions (LODSB, STOSW, ...) have
a big-endian layout under MSB_FIRST, but only the libretro core gets it,
from retro_endianness.h. The SDL2 binary built on a big-endian machine
used the little-endian layout: a byte written to AL landed in the top
byte of EAX, so the font code's offsets went out of range and the game
crashed on its first frames of text (ppc64: segfault in program(), at
LODSB in aff_lettre, ESI 0x481dd440). Define MSB_FIRST from the
compiler's byte order when the libretro header isn't used.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/mrboom.h b/mrboom.h
--- a/mrboom.h
+++ b/mrboom.h
@@ -15,6 +15,11 @@
 #endif
 #else
 #include <stdbool.h>
+/* Only the libretro core gets MSB_FIRST from retro_endianness.h; the SDL
+ * front ends need it too on a big-endian machine. */
+#if !defined(MSB_FIRST) && defined(__BYTE_ORDER__) && __BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__
+#define MSB_FIRST 1
+#endif
 #endif
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
